1
00:05:53,333 --> 00:05:59,333
The end of an empire. The birth of two nations.

2
00:11:46,666 --> 00:11:52,666
Viceroy's House is a drama, history film directed by Gurinder Chadha.

3
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:46,000
In 1947, Lord Mountbatten assumes the post of last Viceroy, charged with handing India back to its people, living upstairs at
the house which was the home of British rulers, whilst 500 Hindu, Muslim and Sikh servants lived downstairs.

4
00:23:33,333 --> 00:23:39,333
Lord Mountbatten, played by Hugh Bonneville.

5
00:29:26,666 --> 00:29:32,666
Edwina Mountbatten, played by Gillian Anderson.

6
00:35:20,000 --> 00:35:26,000
General Hastings Ismay, played by Michael Gambon.

7
00:41:13,333 --> 00:41:19,333
Jeet, played by Manish Dayal.

8
00:47:06,666 --> 00:47:12,666
Aalia, played by Huma Qureshi.

9
00:53:00,000 --> 00:53:06,000
Ewart, played by David Hayman.

10
00:58:53,333 --> 00:58:59,333
Viceroy's House is a 2017 historical drama film directed by Gurinder Chadha
and written by Paul Mayeda Berges, Moira Buffini, and Chadha.

11
01:04:46,666 --> 01:04:52,666
The film stars Hugh Bonneville, Gillian Anderson, Manish
Dayal, Huma Qureshi, and Michael Gambon.

12
01:10:40,000 --> 01:10:46,000
It was selected to be screened out of competition at the
67th Berlin International Film Festival.

13
01:16:33,333 --> 01:16:39,333
The film was released in the United Kingdom on 3 March 2017, while the Hindi dubbed version titled
Partition: 1947 was released in India on 18 August 2017, three days after its 70th Independence Day.

14
01:22:26,666 --> 01:22:32,666
It was released worldwide on 1 September 2017.

15
01:28:20,000 --> 01:28:26,000
Viceroy's House is based on Freedom at Midnight by Larry Collins and Dominique Lapierre, and The
Shadow of the Great Game: The Untold Story of Partition by Narendra Singh Sarila.

16
01:34:13,333 --> 01:34:19,333
The film explores themes of independence, religious
conflict, colonial india, interfaith love.

17
01:40:06,666 --> 01:40:12,666
The tone is emotional.
